51
00:02:59,994 --> 00:03:03,030
let us turn to the investigator
who commanded the task force.

52
00:03:04,030 --> 00:03:07,273
[INVESTIGATOR] When we received
that letter in March 2004,

53
00:03:07,273 --> 00:03:12,402
the first question our task force
posed was not where he was hiding,

54
00:03:12,402 --> 00:03:13,910
but rather: Why now?

55
00:03:14,810 --> 00:03:18,991
And when we reviewed local newspaper
archives from preceding months,

56
00:03:18,991 --> 00:03:22,250
we uncovered the trigger
that sparked his resurgence:

57
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:23,541
In early 2004,

58
00:03:23,541 --> 00:03:27,306
The Wichita Eagle published
a series of articles marking

59
00:03:27,306 --> 00:03:30,600
the thirtieth anniversary
of BTK’s first murders.

60
00:03:30,950 --> 00:03:31,920
In that feature,

61
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:34,952
a local author named Robert
Beattie announced that

62
00:03:34,952 --> 00:03:37,801
he was preparing to
publish a book on the case,

63
00:03:37,801 --> 00:03:42,470
openly questioning whether BTK was dead
or physically incapable of operating.

64
00:03:42,820 --> 00:03:47,523
That proved to be a direct strike
against the killer’s fatal vulnerability:

65
00:03:47,523 --> 00:03:49,780
His pathological narcissistic pride.

66
00:03:50,530 --> 00:03:53,530
He could not endure the thought
of the world forgetting him.

67
00:03:54,580 --> 00:04:00,580
He felt compelled to remind all of humanity:
The monster named BTK was still alive,

68
00:04:00,596 --> 00:04:04,220
and he still commanded the
fear of an entire city.

69
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:08,460
[HOST] Welcome to the criminal
psychology case files.

70
00:04:08,810 --> 00:04:09,153
Today,

71
00:04:09,153 --> 00:04:11,839
we unlock one of the most
thrilling and classic

72
00:04:11,839 --> 00:04:14,810
psychological duels in
modern investigative history:

73
00:04:14,810 --> 00:04:18,010
The file of Dennis Rader—the
man who called himself BTK.

74
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:21,963
This episode will dissect two
dark psychological architectures:

75
00:04:21,963 --> 00:04:26,767
The Malignant Narcissist’s Addiction to
Attention and Absolute Compartmentalization,

76
00:04:26,767 --> 00:04:28,139
addressing the question:

77
00:04:28,139 --> 00:04:30,827
How could an arrogant
ego bring down a flawless

78
00:04:30,827 --> 00:04:32,1000
facade fortified across three decades?

79
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:38,027
[HOST] To grasp the true
nature of Dennis Rader,

80
00:04:38,027 --> 00:04:41,402
we must first examine what he
left behind at crime scenes

81
00:04:41,402 --> 00:04:44,480
throughout seventeen active
years from 1974 to 1991.

82
00:04:44,830 --> 00:04:48,044
Unlike conventional offenders
driven by monetary gain,

83
00:04:48,044 --> 00:04:49,829
revenge, or impulsive passion,

84
00:04:49,829 --> 00:04:54,590
Rader operated with an extraordinary Modus
Operandi and Psychological Signature.

85
00:04:54,940 --> 00:04:57,217
He coined his own moniker: BTK—

86
00:04:57,217 --> 00:05:02,137
an acronym of three English verbs
describing a calculated sequence:

87
00:05:02,137 --> 00:05:03,900
Bind, Torture, and Kill.

88
00:05:04,850 --> 00:05:09,050
Let us invite the Investigator to analyze
this toxic psychological signature.

89
00:05:10,350 --> 00:05:12,038
[INVESTIGATOR] In FBI behavioral science,

90
00:05:12,038 --> 00:05:14,959
a psychological signature
is what an offender

91
00:05:14,959 --> 00:05:17,750
does to satisfy an
internal emotional need,

92
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:21,190
rather than to facilitate
the crime or evade capture:

93
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:25,320
First: The demand for absolute domination.

94
00:05:25,670 --> 00:05:27,630
Rader never acted hastily.

95
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:31,208
He infiltrated victims' homes after dark,

96
00:05:31,208 --> 00:05:34,353
severed telephone lines,
incapacitated his targets,

97
00:05:34,353 --> 00:05:39,040
and bound them with ligatures to render
them completely helpless before him.

98
00:05:39,390 --> 00:05:42,090
He deliberately prolonged
the ordeal to savor

99
00:05:42,090 --> 00:05:44,550
the visceral terror in his victims' eyes.

100
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:48,500
Second: The obsession
with retaining trophies.

101
00:05:49,250 --> 00:05:52,456
He took small personal
belongings from his victims,

102
00:05:52,456 --> 00:05:55,850
such as driver’s licenses,
watches, or modest jewelry.

103
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:58,906
To Rader, these items
held no monetary worth,

104
00:05:58,906 --> 00:06:02,032
but served as psychological
triggers allowing him to

105
00:06:02,032 --> 00:06:05,640
re-experience feelings of
omnipotence whenever he was alone.

106
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:10,070
And third: The impulse for
derisive communication.

107
00:06:10,420 --> 00:06:13,583
He covertly planted parcels
inside public libraries,

108
00:06:13,583 --> 00:06:16,746
taped beneath tables or
tucked into park trash cans,

109
00:06:16,746 --> 00:06:19,605
containing self-authored
poems and word puzzles

110
00:06:19,605 --> 00:06:22,220
directed at police and
television stations.

111
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:27,740
[HOST] A predator meticulous, patient, and
calculating down to the smallest detail.

112
00:06:28,090 --> 00:06:32,482
He was well-versed in police investigative
techniques, consistently wore gloves,

113
00:06:32,482 --> 00:06:36,050
and left behind no discernible
fingerprints or biological traces.

114
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:38,873
Yet what left America
completely dumbfounded on

115
00:06:38,873 --> 00:06:41,241
the day of his arrest
was not the body count,

116
00:06:41,241 --> 00:06:43,240
but the true identity behind his mask.

117
00:06:43,990 --> 00:06:46,473
Let us listen to the
Investigator reconstruct

118
00:06:46,473 --> 00:06:48,790
the mundane civilian life of Dennis Rader.

119
00:06:49,790 --> 00:06:51,890
[INVESTIGATOR] Dennis
Rader was born in 1945,

120
00:06:51,890 --> 00:06:55,320
served four years in the
United States Air Force,

121
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:59,310
and earned a college degree
in Administration of Justice.

122
00:06:59,660 --> 00:07:00,519
For decades,

123
00:07:00,519 --> 00:07:04,812
he lived in a modest home in
Park City alongside his devoted

124
00:07:04,812 --> 00:07:08,820
wife of over thirty years and
two well-behaved children.

125
00:07:09,170 --> 00:07:13,298
He served as President of the Church
Council at Christ Lutheran Church—

126
00:07:13,298 --> 00:07:16,961
standing before the congregation
weekly to welcome worshippers,

127
00:07:16,961 --> 00:07:19,810
collect tithes, and
coordinate charitable events.

128
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:22,117
He served as a Cub Scout leader—

129
00:07:22,117 --> 00:07:25,481
personally teaching neighborhood
boys how to tie knots,

130
00:07:25,481 --> 00:07:27,560
pitch tents, and practice honesty.

131
00:07:27,910 --> 00:07:29,313
And from 1991 onward,

132
00:07:29,313 --> 00:07:34,590
he worked as a Compliance and Animal
Control Officer for the City of Park City.

133
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:37,900
His daily duty entailed
driving an official

134
00:07:37,900 --> 00:07:40,437
city pickup truck along suburban streets,

135
00:07:40,437 --> 00:07:44,583
measuring the height of residential
lawns, capturing stray animals,

136
00:07:44,583 --> 00:07:47,800
and issuing citations to
improperly parked vehicles.

137
00:07:48,450 --> 00:07:51,321
He was strict to the
point of being tyrannical,

138
00:07:51,321 --> 00:07:53,582
meticulous to the point of obsession,

139
00:07:53,582 --> 00:07:57,064
and not a soul in town could
ever have conceived that the

140
00:07:57,064 --> 00:08:00,730
man wielding the lawn-measuring
ruler was the BTK strangler.

141
00:08:02,230 --> 00:08:06,670
[HOST] By day a model citizen, a devout
congregant, a respectable family father.

142
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:11,480
By night a cold-blooded predator extinguishing
the lives of innocent human beings.

143
00:08:12,530 --> 00:08:16,455
How could two such profoundly polarized
personalities coexist in harmony

144
00:08:16,455 --> 00:08:20,490
inside a single human being for more
than thirty years without unraveling?

145
00:08:21,490 --> 00:08:25,810
Let us invite the Psychologist to dissect
this bizarre psychiatric architecture.

146
00:08:28,210 --> 00:08:29,571
[PSYCHOLOGIST] To decode Dennis Rader,

147
00:08:29,571 --> 00:08:33,535
forensic psychologists and
criminologists have analyzed two extreme

148
00:08:33,535 --> 00:08:38,210
psychological defense mechanisms that
defined his entire behavioral repertoire:

149
00:08:38,860 --> 00:08:42,260
The first mechanism: Absolute
Compartmentalization.

150
00:08:42,610 --> 00:08:45,156
Much like the case of
Colonel Russell Williams,

151
00:08:45,156 --> 00:08:48,136
Dennis Rader possessed an
extraordinary ability to seal

152
00:08:48,136 --> 00:08:51,170
off psychological compartments
with absolute perfection.

153
00:08:51,820 --> 00:08:54,716
He erected an impenetrable
concrete wall between his

154
00:08:54,716 --> 00:08:57,780
family and social existence
and his dark fantasy world:

155
00:08:58,130 --> 00:09:01,722
When standing inside the Lutheran
church or mentoring young Scouts,

156
00:09:01,722 --> 00:09:06,010
he fully immersed himself in the persona
of a pious believer and devoted father.

157
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:10,930
He experienced no guilt or remorse,
because in his cognitive processing,

158
00:09:10,930 --> 00:09:14,520
those horrific crimes belonged
to an entirely separate entity.

159
00:09:14,870 --> 00:09:17,793
And to rationalize that
internal fragmentation,

160
00:09:17,793 --> 00:09:22,270
Rader conjured an externalized
delusional concept he labeled: “Factor X.

161
00:09:24,370 --> 00:09:27,010
[HOST] A truly bizarre concept, expert.

162
00:09:27,660 --> 00:09:32,140
Dennis Rader repeatedly referenced this
term “Factor X” in his letters to police.

163
00:09:32,490 --> 00:09:36,490
Under the lens of psychological
science, what was “Factor X” in reality?

164
00:09:37,590 --> 00:09:39,430
[PSYCHOLOGIST] From a
psychological standpoint,

165
00:09:39,430 --> 00:09:43,110
“Factor X” was neither a supernatural
demon nor an occult force.

166
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:48,680
It was an archetypal defense mechanism of
Rationalization and External Projection:

167
00:09:49,030 --> 00:09:53,790
Rader viewed his violent impulses as a
parasitic foreign entity possessing his mind.

168
00:09:54,140 --> 00:09:57,618
He convinced himself: “It was
not that I wanted to do it,

169
00:09:57,618 --> 00:10:00,180
but Factor X inside me forced me to do it.

170
00:10:01,230 --> 00:10:03,973
By offloading culpability
onto an abstract entity,

171
00:10:03,973 --> 00:10:07,155
he completely stripped away
personal moral accountability,

172
00:10:07,155 --> 00:10:10,941
allowing him to gratify his darkest
fantasies while returning home to

173
00:10:10,941 --> 00:10:15,110
embrace his daughter and smile across
the dinner table like an innocent man.

174
00:10:16,310 --> 00:10:19,670
[HOST] A sophisticated rationalization
to lull his own conscience.

175
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:20,932
Yet expert,

176
00:10:20,932 --> 00:10:23,382
if he had successfully
compartmentalized his

177
00:10:23,382 --> 00:10:25,943
mind and safely hibernated
for thirteen years,

178
00:10:25,943 --> 00:10:28,560
why could he not take
that secret to the grave?

179
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:32,720
What motive dragged him back
into this perilous game in 2004?

180
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:36,186
[PSYCHOLOGIST] That brings
us to the second mechanism:

181
00:10:36,186 --> 00:10:39,340
Malignant Narcissism and
the Addiction to Attention.

182
00:10:39,990 --> 00:10:42,359
For a severe narcissist like Dennis Rader,

183
00:10:42,359 --> 00:10:44,953
the sense of control and
the awe of the public

184
00:10:44,953 --> 00:10:47,830
constitute the essential
oxygen sustaining his ego.

185
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:52,909
He did not merely want to commit murder;
he needed the world talking about him,

186
00:10:52,909 --> 00:10:56,160
trembling before him, analyzing
every line of his letters.

187
00:10:56,510 --> 00:10:59,552
Throughout the thirteen
years from 1991 to 2004,

188
00:10:59,552 --> 00:11:04,368
when he ceased offending due to advancing
age and domestic responsibilities,

189
00:11:04,368 --> 00:11:09,501
Rader lived on the reflected glory of his
past: He quietly tracked news coverage,

190
00:11:09,501 --> 00:11:13,430
cutting every clipping regarding
BTK into a private scrapbook.

191
00:11:14,180 --> 00:11:19,245
Yet when The Wichita Eagle published an
article implying BTK was dead or irrelevant,

192
00:11:19,245 --> 00:11:22,380
his narcissistic ego suffered
a catastrophic injury.

193
00:11:23,330 --> 00:11:27,650
The greatest terror for a narcissist
is not incarceration, but Obscurity.

194
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:32,606
He would rather risk capture so the
world could behold his mask than

195
00:11:32,606 --> 00:11:36,000
die in the anonymity of a suburban
municipal compliance officer.

196
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:39,760
[HOST] The addiction to
attention utterly blinded the

197
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:42,020
survival instincts of
an experienced predator.

198
00:11:42,870 --> 00:11:45,733
He believed he was smarter
than the entire police force,

199
00:11:45,733 --> 00:11:48,750
convinced he could orchestrate
the media game indefinitely.

200
00:11:49,100 --> 00:11:51,860
And that blind arrogance
paved the way for Lieutenant

201
00:11:51,860 --> 00:11:54,620
Ken Landwehr to spring a
historic technological trap.

202
00:11:57,120 --> 00:11:58,680
[HOST] Early 2005.

203
00:11:59,330 --> 00:12:02,536
Following a string of mocking
letters mailed to news outlets,

204
00:12:02,536 --> 00:12:05,269
Dennis Rader began growing
weary of manually typing,

205
00:12:05,269 --> 00:12:09,210
assembling parcels, and scouting drop
sites amidst freezing winter weather.

206
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:12,616
He sought to transition to
a more contemporary medium:

207
00:12:12,616 --> 00:12:14,880
Transmitting computerized digital files.

208
00:12:15,230 --> 00:12:16,502
However, at that point,

209
00:12:16,502 --> 00:12:18,880
Rader was sixty years
old and fundamentally

210
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:21,590
ignorant regarding digital
technology principles.

211
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:23,513
On January 8th, 2005,

212
00:12:23,513 --> 00:12:26,606
Dennis Rader slipped a
cereal box onto the bed of a

213
00:12:26,606 --> 00:12:29,880
pickup truck in the Home
Depot parking lot in Wichita.

214
00:12:30,230 --> 00:12:33,799
Inside the cereal box was a
handwritten note addressed to police,

215
00:12:33,799 --> 00:12:36,270
posing an inquiry
astonishing in its naivety:

216
00:12:37,020 --> 00:12:40,300
Can I communicate with a floppy disk
and not be traced to a computer?

217
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:42,220
Be honest.

218
00:12:42,570 --> 00:12:46,168
And he instructed detectives to
reply through a coded message

219
00:12:46,168 --> 00:12:49,530
placed in classified ad section
494 of The Wichita Eagle.

220
00:12:50,730 --> 00:12:54,962
[INVESTIGATOR] When that note was placed
upon the desk of Lieutenant Ken Landwehr—

221
00:12:54,962 --> 00:12:56,730
commander of the task force—

222
00:12:56,730 --> 00:13:01,530
all of us grasped: A once-in-a-thirty-year
opportunity had presented itself.

223
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:05,440
We immediately consulted
digital forensic specialists.

224
00:13:05,790 --> 00:13:06,763
They confirmed:

225
00:13:06,763 --> 00:13:09,681
Any file created on a
computer carries hidden

226
00:13:09,681 --> 00:13:12,470
residual data footprints
known as Metadata.

227
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:17,280
Our investigative team resolved to
deliver a psychological deception:

228
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:22,806
On February 10th, 2005, within the
classifieds of The Wichita Eagle,

229
00:13:22,806 --> 00:13:27,830
a brief notice appeared reading:
“Rex, it will be okay to send it.

230
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:33,260
The narcissist Dennis Rader placed
complete faith in the police’s “assurance.

231
00:13:33,610 --> 00:13:36,713
Six days later, on February 16th, 2005,

232
00:13:36,713 --> 00:13:41,090
a padded package arrived at
television station KSAS-TV.

233
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:46,080
Inside was a purple Memorex
1.44-megabyte floppy disk.

234
00:13:47,580 --> 00:13:49,489
[HOST] The purple floppy
disk was immediately

235
00:13:49,489 --> 00:13:51,700
rushed to the police
digital forensics unit.

236
00:13:52,350 --> 00:13:55,341
Specialist Randy Stone
conducted an exhaustive scan

237
00:13:55,341 --> 00:13:58,390
of the magnetic sectors
utilizing forensic software.

238
00:13:58,740 --> 00:14:01,499
Alongside the visible
file named TestA.rtf,

239
00:14:01,499 --> 00:14:05,220
he recovered a previously
deleted Microsoft Word document.

240
00:14:05,570 --> 00:14:10,450
And within the embedded metadata properties
of that file, two fateful lines emerged:

241
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:14,520
Line one: “Last saved by: Dennis.

242
00:14:15,470 --> 00:14:19,510
Line two: “Company registered:
Christ Lutheran Church.

243
00:14:22,310 --> 00:14:24,236
[INVESTIGATOR] Detectives
immediately typed the

244
00:14:24,236 --> 00:14:26,523
keywords into an online search engine:

245
00:14:26,523 --> 00:14:28,870
“Christ Lutheran Church Wichita Dennis.

246
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:33,393
With a single click, the church’s
official homepage materialized,

247
00:14:33,393 --> 00:14:35,360
presenting its leadership roster:

248
00:14:35,710 --> 00:14:38,830
President of the Church
Council: Dennis Rader.

249
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:43,240
Every puzzle piece across
thirty years clicked into place:

250
00:14:43,590 --> 00:14:46,700
Rader’s black pickup truck
matched the vehicle captured

251
00:14:46,700 --> 00:14:49,470
on surveillance cameras
at parcel drop locations.

252
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:53,574
His residential address at
6220 Independence Street sat

253
00:14:53,574 --> 00:14:56,840
at the geographical center
of the historical crimes.

254
00:14:57,190 --> 00:15:01,621
And to establish absolute biological
DNA certainty prior to making an arrest,

255
00:15:01,621 --> 00:15:04,902
we secured a court warrant to
obtain a pap smear specimen

256
00:15:04,902 --> 00:15:08,470
belonging to Rader’s daughter
from a university health clinic.

257
00:15:08,820 --> 00:15:11,847
DNA comparative analysis
from the state crime

258
00:15:11,847 --> 00:15:14,470
laboratory yielded a 100 percent match:

259
00:15:14,470 --> 00:15:17,968
The familial profile recovered
from BTK crime scenes

260
00:15:17,968 --> 00:15:21,600
belonged to the biological
father of that young woman.

261
00:15:22,350 --> 00:15:23,990
The perimeter was sealed.

262
00:15:25,490 --> 00:15:28,490
[HOST] Midday on February 25th, 2005.

263
00:15:29,140 --> 00:15:33,276
As Dennis Rader was driving his pickup
truck home to share lunch with his wife,

264
00:15:33,276 --> 00:15:36,260
dozens of patrol units converged
and blocked his vehicle.

265
00:15:37,210 --> 00:15:40,450
The sixty-year-old man was
handcuffed in utter bewilderment.

266
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:44,873
Yet the most remarkable moment of judicial
psychology transpired hours later,

267
00:15:44,873 --> 00:15:48,840
when Rader sat opposite Lieutenant Ken
Landwehr in the interrogation suite.

268
00:15:49,940 --> 00:15:53,074
[INVESTIGATOR] Rader looked across
at me with a bewildered expression,

269
00:15:53,074 --> 00:15:55,980
petulant like a child
cheated in a playground game.

270
00:15:56,630 --> 00:15:57,550
He asked:

271
00:15:57,900 --> 00:16:00,340
Ken, I have to ask you one thing...

272
00:16:00,690 --> 00:16:03,370
Why did you lie to me
about the floppy disk?

273
00:16:04,370 --> 00:16:07,490
I looked him straight in
the eyes and replied calmly:

274
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:09,880
Because we were trying to catch you.

275
00:16:10,830 --> 00:16:13,993
A cold-blooded serial
killer who had manipulated

276
00:16:13,993 --> 00:16:17,090
the terror of an entire
state for three decades

277
00:16:17,090 --> 00:16:20,121
felt genuinely aggrieved
simply because police

278
00:16:20,121 --> 00:16:23,350
had broken a promise in
a game of his own making.

279
00:16:23,700 --> 00:16:28,560
And immediately following that response,
recognizing that his mask had shattered,

280
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:32,640
Rader launched into a thirty-hour
monologue detailing every offense,

281
00:16:32,640 --> 00:16:34,020
speaking in a detached,

282
00:16:34,020 --> 00:16:38,100
proud tone akin to a professor
lecturing on his life’s achievements.

283
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:42,369
[HOST] Yet behind the morbid
gratification of the perpetrator

284
00:16:42,369 --> 00:16:45,240
lay the harrowing devastation
of his closest loved ones.

285
00:16:46,090 --> 00:16:48,936
Let us listen to the poignant
words of Kerri Rawson—

286
00:16:48,936 --> 00:16:52,330
Dennis Rader’s biological
daughter—recalling that fateful day.

287
00:16:53,430 --> 00:16:55,790
[KERRI RAWSON] The world knows
him as a barbaric monster.

288
00:16:56,740 --> 00:16:59,720
Yet to me, he was once
the most wonderful father:

289
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:02,153
the man who taught me to ride a bicycle,

290
00:17:02,153 --> 00:17:07,140
took me fishing, walked me down the aisle,
and diligently provided for our family.

291
00:17:08,090 --> 00:17:11,507
When FBI agents knocked on my
door and revealed the truth,

292
00:17:11,507 --> 00:17:14,570
my entire childhood memory
bank collapsed into ruin.

293
00:17:15,620 --> 00:17:19,058
The deepest agony was not discovering
a criminal out in society,

294
00:17:19,058 --> 00:17:21,797
but realizing that the
monster hunted by the entire

295
00:17:21,797 --> 00:17:25,020
nation... was the man who kissed
me goodnight every evening.

296
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:30,000
[HOST] August 18th, 2005.

297
00:17:30,650 --> 00:17:33,290
At the Sedgwick County
District Court in Wichita.

298
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:36,613
Judge Gregory Waller formally
sentenced Dennis Lynn Rader

299
00:17:36,613 --> 00:17:39,483
to ten consecutive life terms
for ten counts of murder,

300
00:17:39,483 --> 00:17:42,195
carrying a minimum mandatory
term of one hundred and

301
00:17:42,195 --> 00:17:44,960
seventy-five years without
any possibility of parole.

302
00:17:46,310 --> 00:17:48,362
At the time Rader committed his crimes,

303
00:17:48,362 --> 00:17:51,572
the State of Kansas had not yet
reinstated the death penalty,

304
00:17:51,572 --> 00:17:53,835
making life imprisonment
without parole the

305
00:17:53,835 --> 00:17:56,150
most severe penalty
available under the law.

306
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:58,174
Today, in his eighties,

307
00:17:58,174 --> 00:18:00,922
Dennis Rader serves his
time inside a solitary

308
00:18:00,922 --> 00:18:04,028
confinement cell at El
Dorado Correctional Facility—

309
00:18:04,028 --> 00:18:06,836
where he remains utterly
isolated from society,

310
00:18:06,836 --> 00:18:10,480
confronting absolute silence
until the final day of his life.

311
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:15,607
[HOST] The BTK file concluded
after more than three decades,

312
00:18:15,607 --> 00:18:19,031
leaving investigators and society
invaluable lessons regarding

313
00:18:19,031 --> 00:18:22,400
the identification of evil
lurking beneath a flawless facade.

314
00:18:23,050 --> 00:18:27,250
Let us invite the Psychologist and
Investigator to synthesize four critical

315
00:18:27,250 --> 00:18:31,450
Red Flags concerning malignant narcissistic
personalities in everyday life.

316
00:18:32,450 --> 00:18:36,530
[PSYCHOLOGIST] The first red flag: Extreme
obsession with enforcing rigid rules.

317
00:18:36,880 --> 00:18:39,676
Exercise caution regarding
individuals who display

318
00:18:39,676 --> 00:18:42,192
a pathological fixation
on petty regulations,

319
00:18:42,192 --> 00:18:44,652
perpetually seeking to
dominate and penalize

320
00:18:44,652 --> 00:18:47,000
others through administrative enforcement.

321
00:18:47,350 --> 00:18:51,310
That frequently signals a deeply
repressed craving for power and control.

322
00:18:52,060 --> 00:18:57,121
The second red flag: Emotional detachment
masked behind outward enthusiasm,

323
00:18:57,121 --> 00:18:58,740
known as Shallow Affect.

324
00:18:59,090 --> 00:19:03,847
A person may vigorously participate in
civic, charitable, or religious endeavors,

325
00:19:03,847 --> 00:19:07,135
yet in substantive interpersonal
relations demonstrate a

326
00:19:07,135 --> 00:19:10,424
complete absence of genuine
empathy for human suffering—

327
00:19:10,424 --> 00:19:12,890
a classic marker of a psychopathic facade.

328
00:19:13,990 --> 00:19:18,990
[INVESTIGATOR] The third red flag: Secret
hoarding of personal belongings of others.

329
00:19:19,340 --> 00:19:23,730
The covert behavior of accumulating
and concealing personal mementos,

330
00:19:23,730 --> 00:19:25,129
identification papers,

331
00:19:25,129 --> 00:19:29,010
or belongings of other people
as symbolic trophies represents

332
00:19:29,010 --> 00:19:32,700
the most alarming indicator
of covert predatory fantasies.

333
00:19:33,050 --> 00:19:38,850
And the fourth red flag: A desperate
narcissistic hunger for validation at any cost.

334
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:44,280
Narcissistic offenders harbor a
bottomless deficit in self-esteem.

335
00:19:44,630 --> 00:19:47,898
They may suppress overt
actions for extensive periods,

336
00:19:47,898 --> 00:19:51,893
but will inevitably betray themselves
and self-destruct when their

337
00:19:51,893 --> 00:19:56,190
arrogant ego is challenged or when
the craving for notoriety reignites.

338
00:19:58,790 --> 00:20:02,208
[HOST] The file on Dennis Rader closes
with a profound message regarding

339
00:20:02,208 --> 00:20:05,310
karmic retribution and the
self-destructive nature of evil.

340
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:08,737
He once believed that
meticulousness, discipline,

341
00:20:08,737 --> 00:20:12,760
and the mask of a pious man would
shield him from justice indefinitely.

342
00:20:13,110 --> 00:20:16,187
Yet an offender can deceive his
neighbors, deceive his family,

343
00:20:16,187 --> 00:20:19,463
and even deceive the justice system
for thirty years... but he can

344
00:20:19,463 --> 00:20:22,590
never deceive the narcissistic
monster dwelling within himself.

345
00:20:23,540 --> 00:20:25,914
It was arrogance, the
addiction to acclaim,

346
00:20:25,914 --> 00:20:28,454
and delusions of omnipotence
that lured Dennis

347
00:20:28,454 --> 00:20:31,049
Rader into the snare of
the purple floppy disk,

348
00:20:31,049 --> 00:20:35,300
turning his proud ego into the very key
that locked away his freedom forever.

349
00:20:36,250 --> 00:20:37,532
Justice may arrive late,

350
00:20:37,532 --> 00:20:41,912
but through the perseverance of law
enforcement and the rigor of forensic science,

351
00:20:41,912 --> 00:20:44,530
darkness must always yield
to the light of truth.

352
00:20:46,830 --> 00:20:49,183
[HOST] Our sincere gratitude
goes to our expert and

353
00:20:49,183 --> 00:20:51,430
investigator for accompanying our program.

354
00:20:51,780 --> 00:20:55,500
Thank you, our listeners, for tuning
into every moment of today’s broadcast.

355
00:20:56,150 --> 00:20:58,669
Remain vigilant, nurture
a compassionate spirit,

356
00:20:58,669 --> 00:21:02,710
and we look forward to meeting you in
our next criminal psychology case file.
